  "term": "schizotypal personality disorder",
  "definition": "Schizotypal personality disorder is a personality disorder marked by unusual patterns of thinking, perception, speech, and behavior, such as magical thinking, suspiciousness, illusions, vague or overly elaborate speech, and socially inappropriate affect or isolation. These features are present but not severe enough to be considered schizophrenia.",
